# Coding & documentation — fieldops-ui

Architecture and import boundaries live in `000-architecture.mdc`. This file covers how code is written and documented inside those layers.

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` in tsconfig. No exceptions. No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow, or generics.
- No non-null assertions (`!`) outside test files. If a value can be undefined, type it as such and handle it.
- Every prop in an exported `*Props` type gets its own `/** ... */` comment directly above the prop — not one comment for the whole interface. Consumers get per-prop autocomplete without opening source.
- Prefer discriminated unions over boolean flag soup for non-trivial internal state machines:
  `{ status: 'idle' } | { status: 'loading' } | { status: 'error'; error: Error }`
  over `{ isLoading: boolean; isError: boolean; error?: Error }`.
- Generic list/select APIs are generic in TypeScript (`<T,>`), not `any[]` with runtime casts.

## React / React Native

- Function components only.
- `forwardRef` on every component that wraps a native pressable or text input so consumers can attach refs for focus management.
- No side effects in render. `useEffect` synchronizes with external systems; derived values are computed inline or with `useMemo`.
- Accessibility props are required on every interactive primitive: `accessibilityRole`, `accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityState`.
- Boolean props are predicates: `isDisabled`, `isLoading` — never treat `undefined` and `false` as different behavioural modes by accident.
- Prefer named exports. One component per file; file name matches the component name.
- No inline object/array literals passed as props in hot paths (list item renderers) — hoist or memoize so memoized rows stay stable.

## Component behaviour contracts

- **Button** — variants `primary` | `secondary` | `ghost` | `destructive`; sizes `sm` | `md` | `lg`; loading and disabled; optional leading icon; `className` + `style`.
- **Text** — typographic scale from tokens (`title` | `heading` | `body` | `label` | `caption`); `className` + `style`.
- **TextField** — label, placeholder, helper text, error state, optional right adornment; usable with a controlled form library (`value` / `onChangeText` or documented equivalents); `className` + `style`.
- **Select** — single-select from options; usable with a long list; error state; `className` + `style`.
- **Badge** — one visual treatment per status tone from the token status map; `className` + `style`.

## Styling in code (enforce with architecture)

- Components obtain default theme styling through `core/integrations/styling` ports and `core/styles` recipes — never by importing NativeWind/Tailwind helpers directly.
- Dual override path (required on public components):
  - `className` — NativeWind hosts; merge via shared `composeClassName` (last-wins per utility group).
  - `style` — all hosts; token StyleSheet defaults + consumer `style` last in the array.
- Behaviour props (`variant`, `size`, `isLoading`, …) stay on the API even when styles are overridden.
- Do not repeat style literals. If two components need the same visual fragment, promote it to `core/styles` (or tokens if it is a raw value) and derive both class and StyleSheet forms from tokens.
- Do not invent one-off theme `style={{ ... }}` with raw hex/spacing in components — use token recipes. Consumer-passed `style` props are fine.

## DRY without speculative abstraction

- Duplication across two call sites is acceptable. On the third, extract into `core/styles`, `core/logic`, or an integration port.
- Do not invent a generic abstraction for a single use site.
- Shared behaviour that is not third-party isolation belongs in `core/logic` or `core/styles`, not in a random `utils/` dump that bypasses layering.

## Lint & format

- ESLint with type-aware TypeScript rules and `eslint-plugin-react-hooks`.
- Prettier owns formatting — do not bikeshed style in review.
- Do not silence lint with `eslint-disable` as a first resort. Fix the issue; only disable with a comment that explains a true false positive.

## Documentation — public API

Use full TSDoc on every exported component, prop type, hook, and public utility:

```ts
/**
 * Pressable button with token-driven variants and sizes.
 *
 * Consumer `className` overrides internal utilities through the shared merge
 * strategy (last-wins on conflicting utility groups). Consumer `style`
 * overrides token StyleSheet defaults (RN array last-wins).
 *
 * @remarks
 * Forwards its ref to the underlying `Pressable`. Styling goes through the
 * integrations styling port — this file must not import NativeWind directly.
 *
 * @example
 * ```tsx
 * <Button variant="primary" onPress={handleSubmit} isLoading={isSubmitting}>
 *   Save
 * </Button>
 * ```
 */
export const Button = forwardRef<View, ButtonProps>(...)
```

- `@example` is required on each of the five public components and must match the README usage example.
- `@remarks` covers non-obvious behaviour: dual style path, merge strategy, ref forwarding, controlled state, composable escape hatch.
- README: install steps + one usage example per component. README is task-oriented; TSDoc is API-reference-oriented — do not paste one into the other wholesale.

## Documentation — internal logic (required)

Document non-trivial internal functions in **both** places:

1. **Above the function** — short block stating purpose and why this approach (trade-off, platform or layer constraint).
2. **Inside the function** — inline `//` on non-obvious branches, loops, merges, or early returns. Explain reasoning, not a narration of obvious code.

```ts
/**
 * Merges default recipe classes with consumer overrides.
 * Lives in integrations so components never import the merge library directly.
 */
export function composeClassName(...inputs: ClassValue[]): string {
  // Conflicting utilities must resolve by utility group, not string order alone;
  // otherwise consumer overrides can be silently dropped after NativeWind resolves classes.
  return mergeFn(inputs);
}
```

Skip noise on one-line obvious helpers. Prefer signal over volume.

## Decisions

When choosing merge strategy, composable component, Select long-list approach, or any dependency adapter shape, update `docs/decisions.md` in the same turn per `030-decisions.mdc` (usually §1 defend; NativeWind/preset work also fills §2; deliberate non-builds fill §3).
